\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Croatia cenbank buys 345.5 mln euros from banks in  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 207 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 2017\par 11:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes)               \par \par \uc2 ZAGREB, Dec 13 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Croatia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it bought 345.5 million euros ($405.82 million) from commercial banks on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent appreciation pressures on the kuna \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 It bought the euros at an average rate of 7.5605 kuna per euro. The kuna eased after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 7.5533 per euro at 1035 GMT, easing from around 7.53 before it.               \par \par \uc2 "There were some mild appreciation pressures on the kuna and apparently the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted to act preventively," a dealer at a major local bank said.               \par \par \uc2 Another market participant, who asked not to be named, said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have also wanted to give a boost to its own balance sheet at the end of the year.               \par \par \uc2 This was the fifth \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year to counter appreciation pressures on the kuna and the biggest one in volume. In those five \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  it altogether bought 947 million euros from commercial banks.               \par \par \uc2 In October Croatia tentatively set a goal of adopting the euro within seven to eight years.                              \par \par