\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 3-Zloty leads  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  bounce,  \highlight22\uc2 Croatia \highlight\uc2  cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 917 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2012\par 16:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Romanian leu moves away from all-time low\par \par \uc2 * Stocks, bonds mixed as some Europe markets on holiday\par \par \uc2 * Hungary c.bank seen on hold while volatility persists\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Croatia\b0 \highlight\uc2  c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support kuna\par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 Croatia\b0 \highlight\uc2  details, comment)\par \par \uc2 By Jason Hovet and Sam Cage\par \par \uc2 PRAGUE/BUCHAREST, May 28 (Reuters) - Poland's zloty led central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher on Monday when investors dipped back into the region's riskier assets, though dealers said it was a short-term rebound and expectations of a rally looked misplaced.\par \par \uc2 Opinion polls on Saturday showed Greek conservatives regaining a lead that would allow the formation of a government that supports the country's international bailout, a commitment needed to keep the funds flowing.\par \par \uc2 With Europe's leaders now openly debating a possible exit of Greece from the euro zone, emerging EU assets have taken a beating this month due to the region's close banking, financing and export ties.\par \par \uc2 Markets are tipped to remain volatile until at least June 17, when Greeks vote again to choose a government that will largely determine if the country sticks with the euro.\par \par \uc2 By 1309 GMT the zloty, the region's most liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was bid 0.4 percent higher at 4.336 per euro.\par \par \uc2 The Romanian leu gained 0.3 percent to 4.467 after hitting a record low of 4.50 in late trade on Friday when the wealthiest Spanish region of Catalonia said it needed help with financing, showing the spread of the debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 The threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  away from lows was keeping the market on alert, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 "Overall it resembles more a relief rally in risky assets rather than a new trend," said one.\par \par \uc2 Stocks were mixed, with Bucharest a touch lower around a four-month low due to Romania's large exposure to Greece and Warsaw up 0.9 percent.\par \par \uc2 "Greek polls boosted sentiment, but we're not really seeing a significant increase in demand for riskier assets. It's more of a correction," said a Warsaw-based dealer\par \par \uc2 HUNGARY RATE CALL\par \par \uc2 Trading was muted with the U.S. and some major European centres closed for a holiday. In the debt market, Czech bond yields dipped, getting support from expectations of a rate cut in June. Polish yields were flat.\par \par \uc2 The Czech crown rose 0.3 percent and Hungary's forint, the most vulnerable in the region due to delays in getting an international credit line to help ease debt costs, rose 0.2 percent to in offshore trade with Budapest markets closed.\par \par \uc2 It has rebounded 2 percent since hitting a four-month low in the middle of last week.\par \par \uc2 The market turmoil is putting many central banks in a tight spot by impeding the reduction of interest rates that would help spur the economy.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keep its growth-choking 7 percent base rate on hold on Tuesday, but they said the rate could be cut by 50 basis points by the end of the year if Hungary secures a loan from the International Monetary Fund and EU through talks that have been help up by policy disputes.\par \par \uc2 Croatia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 266.4 million euros to commercial banks to prop up the kuna, which has come under mounting pressure in recent days as demand for euros from local banks has escalated, its fourth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was bid 0.2 percent higher at 7.559 per euro, still weaker than the range of 7.50-7.55 in recent weeks under its managed float system.\par \par \uc2 "Despite this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ... the kuna may remain exposed to depreciation pressures if demand for euros does not subside," a \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealer at a major bank said.  \tab \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2012 \par Czech crown                  25.297    25.362  +0.26%   +0.98%\par Polish zloty                 4.336    4.355  +0.44%   +2.97%\par Hungarian forint             298.6    299.25  +0.22%   +5.36%\par Croatian kuna                7.559    7.57  +0.15%    -0.57%\par Romanian leu                 4.467    4.479  +0.27%    -3.27%\par Serbian dinar                115.97    115.58   -0.34%    -7.78%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds           \par 2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR    -1 basis points to  105bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ6YT=RR    -4 basis points to  +147bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   CZ10YT=RR    0 basis points to  +235bps over bmk*\par Polish treasury bonds           \par 2-yr T-bond   PL2YT=RR   +2 basis points to  +474bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   PL5YT=RR   +1 basis points to  +451bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond PL10YT=RR    0 basis po