\par\par \b \uc2 Croatia cenbank calls auction to tame kuna gains\b0\par\par\uc2 156 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 2009\par 10:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 ZAGREB, Oct 22 (Reuters) - The Croatian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called an auction on Thursday to buy euros from commercial banks in its second effort this month to ease appreciation pressures on the national kuna \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The kuna was quoted at 7.21 per euro before the auction, which will close at 0845 GMT.\par \par \uc2 The market had anticipated a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The kuna has in recent days been exposed to appreciation pressures as banks have been adjusting hard-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions ahead of upcoming borrowing abroad by the government and some state agencies.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  two weeks ago to tame upward pressures on the kuna by buying 154 million euros.\par \par \uc2 This is the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fourth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year to counter kuna gains. It has also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice to boost the kuna.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 CROATIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091022e5am000rz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
