\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 4- \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  rebound on stocks, Polish cbank comments\b0\par\par\uc2 977 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2009\par 16:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  mixed, mkt digests rate comments, decisions\par \par \uc2 * More weakening likely, say dealers\par \par \uc2 * Polish cbank does not rule out future \b \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Croatia\b0 \highlight\uc2  unveils anti-crisis package\par \par \uc2 (Adds new comments, fresh prices.)\par \par \uc2 By Sandor Peto and Dagmara Leszkowicz\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST/WARSAW, Feb 26 (Reuters) - Central Europe's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  inched up late on Thursday, bolstered by a cautious rise in global investors' appetite for risk and comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor.\par \par \uc2 A rise by equities in Europe and a positive opening of stocks in the U.S. gave support to \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the emerging region, helping erase earlier losses for the Polish zloty <EURPLN=>.\par \par \uc2 The zloty also drew some strength, dealers said, from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Slawomir Skrzypek, who said the bank might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the zloty in certain conditions. [ID:nLQ831361]\par \par \uc2 But markets are sceptical on the chances of outright \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks at these levels, and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed in relatively tight ranges after recent sharp losses.\par \par \uc2 The zloty and the Romanian leu were flat against the euro at 1506 GMT at 4.692 and 4.286, respectively, while the Czech crown<EURCZK=> firmed 0.29 percent to 28.289. The Hungarian forint<EURHUF=> and the Croatian kuna<EURHRK=> both gained half a percent, to 299.63 and 7.35, after Croatia's government unveiled measures to counter the impacts of the global crisis.\par \par \uc2 Dealers and strategists said all would remain under pressure as the global crisis hits the region's export-heavy economies and concerns persist over their reliance on foreign financing.\par \par \uc2 "The trend (of weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) hasn't changed really so the recent strengthening could be a short-term correction," said Sylwester Brzeczkowski, dealer at ABN Amro in Warsaw.\par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue to slide, a key question is what governments and central banks in the region are ready to add to Monday's coordinated verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks in the region.\par \par \uc2 The Polish government has moved the zloty by selling some of its EU fund inflows on the open market, and Czech Finance Minister Miroslav Kalousek said late on Wednesday that the government was considering all possible tools to help the undervalued crown.[ID:nLP635129]\par \par \uc2 DILEMMA\par \par \uc2 Poland's quarter-point interest rate cut on Wednesday highlighted the dilemma of banks which have been cutting rates to help the ailing economies but are worried lower interest rates -- which also cuts the premium paid for held assets -- could fuel more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments referring to further rate cuts weakened the Polish unit (on Wednesday), which counters Monday's coordinated regional \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement," Hungarian MKB Bank said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its rates on hold at its meeting early this week, pausing in its earlier monetary easing cycle due to concerns over the forint's weakness and its impact on the loan portfolio quality of domestic banks.\par \par \uc2 But the woes of the economy maintain pressure on the bank to cut interest rates further. Rate setter Julia Kiraly said there were downside risks to its forecasts for growth, which already predict a recession in 2009 and 2010 [ID:nLP831873].\par \par \uc2 The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lowered borrowing costs by a total of 200 basis points in the current easing cycle, bringing the key interest rate to 4.0 percent.\par \par \uc2 However Wednesday's cut was not as sharp as the previous ones, as the council pointed to recent zloty weakening and concerns over its volatility. [ID:nLP445602]\par \par \uc2 "While the sell-off has so far been indiscriminate and Emerging Europe assets are likely to remain under pressure for some time, past episodes show that market moves should eventually reflect country-specific conditions," said Neil Shearing, analyst at Capital Economics in a note.\par \par \uc2 Analysts view Poland and Czech Republic as being in better position to manage the global downturn than states like Romania or Hungary, which have ran higher current account deficits. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ----------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT-------------------------\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2009 \par  Czech crown      <EURCZK=>  28.289   28.37   +0.29%    -5.43%\par  Polish zloty     <EURPLN=>   4.692    4.692   0%      -12.3%\par  Hungarian forin