\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Croat kuna eases after cenbank buys euros   \b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2008\par 11:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds result of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )   \par \par \uc2 ZAGREB, Jan 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Croatia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had bought 189.1 million euros from banks at an average rate of 7.2458 kuna per euro at an auction on Thursday intended to ease upward pressure on the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 After the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which the market largely expected, the kuna eased slightly to 7.2120/7.2180 per euro on the open interbank market from 7.2085/7.2185 in the morning -- its highest level since 2002.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be enough to restrain the kuna this week.   \par \par \uc2 "But next week's (rate) movements depend on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds its weekly reverse repo auction on Wednesday," said a money market dealer from a local bank.   \par \par \uc2 The central has held only one reverse repo auction so far this year, saying it would hold the auctions when it deems necessary, instead of every week, to manage liquidity and the exchange rate.   \par \par \uc2 Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first this year to counter upward pressures on the kuna. Last year it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  four times to cap the kuna, buying altogether 662 million euros from commercial banks.   \par \par \uc2 The kuna has firmed steadily after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Zeljko Rohatinski said last week the bank, prompted by inflationary pressures, would not allow the kuna to depreciate but controlled appreciation pressures were possible.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which keeps the kuna in a managed float, has never publicly said which floating band it targets, but analysts believe it is allowing the band to gradually move upwards.   \par \par \uc2 In the last few months, the kuna mostly traded at between 7.30 and 7.35 to the euro. By contrast, it floated at between 7.5 and 7.7. to the euro several years ago.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CROATIA/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080131e41v0017b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
