\par\par \b \uc2 Croat c.bank moves to halt kuna,money rates steady  \b0\par\par\uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2006\par 11:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 ZAGREB, Nov 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Croatia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday morning to stop appreciation pressure on the kuna.  \par \par \uc2 The bank offered to buy euros from banks after the kuna touched the level of 7.31/7.32 per euro on the open interbank market. The kuna eased immediately to 7.33/7.34 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced the auction.  \par \par \uc2 "We expected the auction because foreign investors need the kuna for buying (state oil concern) INA shares. I think the amount will be quite large but the rate will remain around these levels through this week," said a dealer at a major bank.  \par \par \uc2 Croatia will list 15 percent of INA on Zagreb and London exchanges on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 (For the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's kuna mid-rates click on <HNBZH> after 1230 GMT).  \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry said it would not hold its regular weekly auction of T-bills due to good liquidity.  \par \par \uc2 On the money market, the benchmark overnight lending rate <ZIBOR01> inched down one basis point to 1.52 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Market participants said they expected the overnight lending rate to remain at the current low level until the end of the mandatory reserve maintenance period.  \par \par \uc2 Two bonds traded on the local bond market in the morning on a combined turnover of some 26.7 million kuna ($4.79 million).  \par \par \uc2 Live bond trade on <0#HRTSY=ZA>.  \par \par \uc2 Live corporate bond trade on <0#HRCORP=ZA>.  \par \par \uc2 CROATIA-MARKETS|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|