\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Croat cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to curb kuna strength  \b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juni 2006\par 15:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst quotes, details)  \par \par \uc2 ZAGREB, June 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Croatia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  staged its heaviest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday to curb the pressures on the local kuna \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate.  \par \par \uc2 The bank said it had bought 104.3 million euros from banks at an average rate of 7.258188 kuna per euro at an auction. Its dollar purchases were greater than on any of the five occasions earlier this year when it stepped into the market.  \par \par \uc2 The kuna<EURHRK=> inched down to 7.2528/7.2628 to the euro from a five-year high of 7.2490/7.2570, where it had stood before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which did not surprise the market despite its unusual timing.  \par \par \uc2 "The timing of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Friday afternoon, may be indicative as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  normally did not use to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this time. It may show its determination to keep the kuna at the current level," a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a major local bank said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has intensified \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in recent weeks amid steady appreciation pressures on the kuna. However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have had only a short-term effect.  \par \par \uc2 "Appreciation pressures are strong and steady as there is strong credit activity based on funds from abroad, besides foreign investments and rising tourist income," the dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 This year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought altogether 407.5 million euros from commercial banks in its six \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the kuna.  \par \par \uc2 The previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place on May 15 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought 69.6 million euros at an average rate of 7.275064 kuna per euro.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Zeljko Rohatinski said last month the bank would react strongly if faced with considerable appreciation pressures, but did not elaborate what measures it could take on top of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the kuna to firm further as the tourist summer season gets into full swing and inflow of euros, as well as demand for the kuna, intensifies.  \par \par \uc2 They say steady appreciation pressures are almost certain as the country nears EU membership, adding that the kuna might firm to as much as 7.10 per -euro or even beyond in the coming years.  \par \par \uc2 Croatia opened talks on EU membership with Brussels last October.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CROATIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060602e2620012r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
