\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Croatia c.bank buys 35.5 mln euros to tame kuna  \b0\par\par\uc2 373 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2006\par 12:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds dealer's comment, new rate)  \par \par \uc2 ZAGREB, Feb 2 (Reuters) - Croatia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had bought 35.5 million euros from banks at its auction on Thursday at an average rate of 7.348358 kuna per euro, in its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year to tame the kuna's gains.  \par \par \uc2 The kuna <EURHRK=> eased to 7.35/7.36 from 7.33/7.34 per euro after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but then again inched up to 7.34/7.35.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was no surprise to the market which did not expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to allow the kuna to firm strongly beyond the 7.35 per euro.  \par \par \uc2 "I'm not sure that the amount bought will suffice to stop the appreciation pressures. Maybe the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has come a bit too late when the kuna has already reached the 7.33 level," a dealer at a major local bank said.  \par \par \uc2 The kuna has been floating at between 7.35 and 7.42 versus the euro since Croatia opened European Union entry talks last October but this week it strengthened beyond the 7.35 rate for the first time since last summer.  \par \par \uc2 A year ago the kuna had stood at around 7.50 to the euro, but analysts told Reuters this week that steady appreciation pressures on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are very likely as the country nears EU membership.  \par \par \uc2 They said that the kuna might firm to as high as 7.25 per euro this summer and possibly towards 7.10 or even beyond in the coming years.  \par \par \uc2 The current appreciation pressures are due to strong inflow of euros which local demand cannot match.  \par \par \uc2 The previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place in late December when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought 161.9 million euros at an average rate of 7.390784 kuna per euro.  \par \par \uc2 In last year's nine \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the kuna the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a total of 570.8 million euros from commercial banks.  \par \par \uc2 Unlike in the past, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2005 did not have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the kuna.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 CROATIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060202e222000vh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
