\par\par \b \uc2 Croat kuna seen firming as EU entry nears-analysts  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Igor Ilic  \par \uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2006\par 10:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 ZAGREB, Feb 1 (Reuters) - Croatia's kuna \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to appreciate steadily as the former Yugoslav republic moves towards European Union membership, analysts said on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps the kuna in a managed float regime and until last year it had strengthened in the summer months, amid strong inflow of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from tourism, before gradually easing during the winter season.  \par \par \uc2 A year ago it traded around 7.51/7.52 per euro, but has held at stronger levels since Zagreb opened EU entry talks last October. On Wednesday morning it traded at 7.34/7.35 on the open interbank market.  \par \par \uc2 "Inflows of foreign capital as we approach the EU support a strong kuna," said Mladen Smiljanic of Zagrebacka Banka.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will certainly act to keep appreciation under control," Smiljanic said, but he added that it was not unimaginable to see the kuna firming towards 7.10 per euro in the coming years.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  never publicised its targeted exchange rate band, but it was widely thought that it tolerated a five percent floating band ranging from 7.30 in the summer to 7.70 in the winter season.  \par \par \uc2 In the last few months, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  each time when the kuna was threatening to pierce the 7.35 support level, but this week it let it slip.  \par \par \uc2 "The banks mostly adhered to that level as they deemed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  imminent if they should breach it. The kuna could firm towards 7.25 per one euro this summer, but a lot depends on how the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will react," said Hrvoje Dolenec, an analyst at Raiffeisenbank.  \par \par \uc2 ROOM FOR GAINS  \par \par \uc2 Lars Christensen of Danske Bank said current appreciation pressures reflected positive sentiment on the international markets, as investors expect Croatia to join the EU before the end of the decade.  \par \par \uc2 "There is substantial room for kuna gains against the euro. If there were a free float, the kuna would be considerably stronger. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not allow it, but gradual easing of the (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) policy is possible," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Croatian exporters have often complained that too strong a kuna was hampering their business and voiced dissatisfaction with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exchange rate policy.  \par \par \uc2 But a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  source recently told Reuters that it had acted to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  climbing much faster and further.  \par \par \uc2 "Through our \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market, we prevent the kuna from appreciating more than is actually the case," the source said.  \par \par \uc2 Last year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought 570.8 million euros ($692.2 million) from commercial banks in nine \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the kuna.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-\b \highlight22\uc2 CROATIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -KUNA|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060201e221000oz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
