\par\par \b \uc2 Croatia c.bank buys 162 mln euros to tame kuna  \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2005\par 11:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 ZAGREB, Dec 27 (Reuters) - Croatia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had bought 161.9 million euros from banks at an auction on Tuesday at an average rate of 7.390784 kuna per euro, in an effort to stop the kuna \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent gains versus the euro.  \par \par \uc2 It is the highest amount of euros bought by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year.  \par \par \uc2 The kuna eased to 7.38/7.39 from 7.36/7.37 per one euro after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It was floating at between 7.35 and 7.42 versus the euro since Croatia opened the European Union entry talks in early October.  \par \par \uc2 Market participants said they expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had indicated it did not prefer at the current period to see the kuna stronger than the 7.35 level against the euro.  \par \par \uc2 This time the appreciation pressures were caused by strong inflow of euros on the local market following intensive corporate borrowing abroad in recent days.  \par \par \uc2 The previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place in mid-October when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called an auction when the kuna was quoted at the same level as this morning.  \par \par \uc2 This was the ninth \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year aimed at curbing kuna. In those nine \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a total of 570.8 million euros ($677.1 million) from commercial banks.  \par \par \uc2 Unlike in the past, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year did not have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the kuna.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 CROATIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051227e1cr000er\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
