\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Croatia \highlight\uc2  ZIBOR money rates fall, cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2003\par 15:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ZAGREB, Feb 21 (Reuters) - Ten leading Croatian banks further lowered rates in their direct deals  on Friday amid improved liquidity, with the benchmark overnight rate falling to 1.93 percent from 2.05 percent. \par \par \uc2  On the open interbank market the kuna  eased to 7.61/7.64 from 7.60/7.61 against the euro. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called a tender to sell euros to banks to prop up the kuna after it slid to 7.63/7.64 per one euro in the morning trade. The results of the tender will be released later today. \par \par \uc2  "High demand for euros lies behind the current depreciation of the kuna. Such trend is nothing unusual for this part of the year but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is imminent if the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to slide," said earlier a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  The kuna pierced the psychological level of 7.60 per one euro on Tuesday after floating just under for almost two weeks. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice last month to support the kuna. \par \par \uc2  Its own kuna mid-rates, which reflect market moves with a two-day delay, further eased to 7.6024 from 7.6005 against the euro but firmed to 7.0191 from 7.0597 against the dollar. Other kuna crosses on page . \par \par \uc2  Bond trade by the early afternoon hours was livelier than the previous days with 4.5 million euros ($4.88 million) in turnover in spite of only two government papers traded. More liquid was 10-year finance ministry's bond RHMF-12 with 3.3 million euros of turnover, quoted at 5.45/5.48. The rest went to state banking agency's DAB-05, trading at 3.72/3.77. \par \par \uc2  February is likely to be a month with the lowest turnover since last August. \par \par \uc2  "Investors focused on the three primary emissions taking place in the relatively short period of time with a combined value of 1.0 billion euros. It made trade on the secondary market considerably slower," said a dealer at a major Croatian bank. \par \par \uc2  Third tranche of the RHMF-12 was issued in late January. It was followed by the road constructor Bina Istra corporate bonds and a new issue of Croatian Eurobonds with 7-year maturity. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held its weekly auction of bills denominated in euros and dollars. See page  for details. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030221dz2l00sec\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
