\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Croatia \highlight\uc2  ZIBOR money rates fall, cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2003\par 15:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ZAGREB, Jan 31 (Reuters) - Ten leading Croatian banks further lowered their rates quoted in direct deals  on Friday, with the benchmark overnight rate dropping to 1.63 percent from 1.87 percent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 41.1 million euros ($44.47 million) to banks in an effort to stop a fall in thel kuna. For details see . \par \par \uc2  After the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the kuna  marginally eased to 7.56/7.58 against the euro in interbank deals from 7.57/7.58 where it stood in the morning hours. \par \par \uc2  "Although the amount sold was not very high, I believe the depreciation of the kuna will now stop," a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  The national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's depreciation accelerated in the last week of January, pushing it towards a one-year low against the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held its weekly auction of bills denominated in euros and dollars. See details on . \par \par \uc2  Its own kuna mid-rates, which reflect market moves with a two-day delay, firmed to 7.5458 from 7.5558 against the euro and to 6.9771 from 7.0352 against the dollar. Other kuna crosses on . \par \par \uc2  The local bond market was rather quiet as most dealers and market makers focused on the presentation of road company Bina Istra's 20-year 210 million euro eurobond, lead managed by UBS Warburg and local Zagrebacka Banka. \par \par \uc2  "Books are being closed and the issue is already oversubscribed," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The bond is due to be listed on the Luxembourg and Zagreb stock exchanges on February 14, most probably at 325-375 basis points over the German Bund DBR 6% 06/16. \par \par \uc2  Only two government bonds were traded on the local market with a combined turnover of 2.5 million euros. \par \par \uc2  State health fund's paper HZZO recorded a turnover of 1.5 million, trading at 107.15/107.45, while the long-term government bond RMHF-12, with one million, traded at 110.20/110.50, both with virtually flat yields. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030131dz1v00qjm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
