\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Croatia \highlight\uc2  c.bank to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to support kuna if necessary. \b0\par\par\uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2003\par 14:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ZAGREB, Jan 28 (Reuters) - The Croatian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it was closely watching the kuna's steady depreciation this month and would not hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain its stability. \par \par \uc2  The kuna , which has fallen to an 11-month low, was quoted at 7.56/7.57 against the euro on the interbank market on Tuesday. Its depreciation has accelerated since January 15 when it stood at 7.47/48 per euro. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on January 7 when it sold 74.6 million euros to banks at a fixed 7.52 kuna. \par \par \uc2  Deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Boris Vujcic told Reuters the depreciation was seasonal and typical for the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  "We always have depreciation at this time of the year so this is nothing out of the ordinary framework of the exchange rate movements," he said. \par \par \uc2  Demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rises substantially in January, mostly because of foreign debt servicing, both corporate and government. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be watching the rate to assess if and when to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We have all the instruments to control the exchange rate at our disposal and we shall continue to use them when needed," Vujcic added. \par \par \uc2  Some observers ascribed the depreciation - on top of strong hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand by corporate clients - to commercial banks' efforts to build a long hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  position before a new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rule on asset/liability ratios takes effect in February. \par \par \uc2  The ratio will now be monitored every day instead of the previous practice of monitoring it only once a month. Some banks have met the ratio by taking out short-term loans abroad and then repaying them. \par \par \uc2  Vujcic said it was too early to assess the effects of the new measure. "We will need to follow the trends in the next few months to evaluate their effect". \par \par \uc2  A dealer said that after banks have built up larger hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions to meet the new rule "the effect on the exchange rate will diminish." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has maintained monetary stability since slashing hyperinflation in 1993, has a managed float regime, whereby it keeps the kuna within a desirable band to the euro, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when necessary. \par \par \uc2  "We don't announce the band and don't have a targeted band. We assess the exchange rate, as well as macro and micro economic indicators, at every moment to decide when an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is necessary," Vujcic said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030128dz1s00rmv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
