\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW-Croatian c.bank sees no need to fix kuna. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kolumbina Bencevic \par \uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2001\par 15:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ZAGREB, May 21 (Reuters) - The Croatian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees no need to change the course of its policy or fix the kuna, although its rally threatens to undermine the impending tourist season, governor Zeljko Rohatinski said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Fixing the kuna would make no sense. It would be a move directed against the market. It would not work," Rohatinski told Reuters in an interview. \par \par \uc2  The current exchange rate is a managed float, determined by the market, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to iron out oscillations that are too strong or bear on other developments. \par \par \uc2  The kuna fluctuates seasonally, appreciating on the inflow of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from privatisation, state borrowings abroad and earnings from the flagship tourist trade during the summer. \par \par \uc2  It has hit a three-year peak of 7.3 to the euro this week, after firming more and earlier than usual on proceeds from two foreign debt issues in March. \par \par \uc2  A switch in Croatian banks' investment, due to a global fall of interest rates, from foreign deposits into credits to local borrowers has also contributed. Year-to-April money supply rose some 36 percent and bank credits to the corporate and private borrowers 17 percent. \par \par \uc2  "These are positive and welcome developments," Rohatinski said, adding they were partly a result of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gradual cuts in the banks' mandatory reserves since last year. \par \par \uc2  "So there is no need or possibility to change the exchange rate regime with a satisfactory outcome, while maintaining the same monetary policy course." \par \par \uc2  NO BOWING TO PRESSURE \par \par \uc2  Last week, businessmen and tourism officials complained against the kuna strength and called on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the summer to help \b \highlight22\uc2 Croatia\b0 \highlight\uc2  gain some competitive advantage over other regional destinations. \par \par \uc2  "Such positions of these and other export-oriented companies are understandable and legitimate," Rohatinski said. \par \par \uc2  "But there is a difference between hotel competitiveness, as their prices are for the most part agreed in advance and expressed in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  anyway, and spending on other services outside hotels which may indeed be adversely affected. \par \par \uc2  "However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and exchange rate movements cannot be determined from the aspect of just one branch of the economy or one region," he added. \par \par \uc2  There have also been suggestions from banking circles to introduce the euro as a new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the governor also ruled these out as "unilateral moves that would not help Croatia's bid to join the European Union". \par \par \uc2  Instead, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board last week approved a further cut in the reserve ratio for banks to 22 percent from July to increase kuna liquidity. \par \par \uc2  At the same time it expanded the reserve base by including additional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds to also reduce their supply. \par \par \uc2  But further action is to some extent limited by the fact that two thirds of the broadest monetary aggregate, the M4, are euro funds. They represent a high 80 percent of all deposits. \par \par \uc2  "Such conditions...are practically tying our hands and limiting further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Rohatinski said. \par \par \uc2  The bank now planned to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  through minor foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases to iron out the exchange rate fluctuations without risking the creation of inflationary pressure by pumping in too much money. \par \par \uc2  "It would be a vicious circle of the kind we have seen in the past," Rohatinski said. "It would not do to prevent the kuna appreciation by issuing so much money to cause inflation, and end up 'sinking the drowning man'." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx5l03bwh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
