\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Croatia \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market. \b0\par\par\uc2 186 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ZAGREB, May 20 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Croatia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by buying and selling German marks. \par \par \uc2  "We had two goals: to prevent (the kuna) exchange rate appreciation due to stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflow and to help liquidity of the money market," a bank official told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The bank bought 11.1 million marks at an average rate of 3.5700 kuna, it said in a statement faxed to Reuters. \par \par \uc2  This will result in an injection of just under 40 million kuna into the hard-pressed banking sector in two days. But there was no immediate reaction from the money market. \par \par \uc2  The official said this type of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be more frequent during the summer as more hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from tourism createS an increased demand for kuna by banks and exchange offices, boosting upward pressure on the kuna rate. \par \par \uc2  The bank today also sold two million marks at the same average rate of 3.5700 kuna per mark, it said. \par \par \uc2  -- Kolumbina Bencevic, Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5k05e46\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
